{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Esterification of oleic acid: response surface study",
  "notes": "Batch esterification of oleic acid with 2-ethylhexanol in toluene with p-toluenesulfonic acid as catalyst and azeotropic water removal (Dean-Stark trap). Jacket temperature, reaction time and catalyst loading are optimised with a rotatable central composite design with six centre points, run in random order in a 2 L jacketed reactor. The water content of the oleic acid feedstock is not controlled; it is measured by Karl Fischer titration before each batch and recorded as an environmental factor. A new feedstock drum was opened partway through the campaign. Ester yield is determined by GC against an internal standard, the bis(2-ethylhexyl) ether by-product as GC area %, and the colour of the crude product on the platinum-cobalt (APHA) scale.",
